## Vendored upstream: flydev-fr/mormot.ai  (code adoption, NOT a fork)

We adopt CODE only — no shared repository, no fork, no upstream PRs. Our namespace
`mormot.ai.*` stays as-is even where it collides with theirs (CONCEPT.md §1/§4);
adopted units are renamed/aligned into our tree.

Tracking the base commit is what makes incremental updates possible: to pull later
changes, diff THEIR repo between the pinned commit and their new HEAD, port what is
relevant, then bump the commit below.

  Project: flydev-fr/mormot.ai   (library: mormot2-pgvector)
  URL:     https://github.com/flydev-fr/mormot.ai
  Branch:  main
  Commit:  9ab26e88171c98a24ae64fcdc75866440b7518a4   <-- BASELINE, not yet adopted
  Date:    2026-07-28   ("chore: README")
  License: MIT  (mormot2-pgvector/LICENSE) — copyright notice must be retained.
  Scope:   mormot.ai.chunk, mormot.ai.embed.{base,ollama}, mormot.ai.llm.{base,ollama},
           mormot.ai.rag.{history,service,stream}, mormot.db.pgvector.{binding,orm,base}

  BLOCKED — do not adopt: the second library `mormot-ai-sdk` (LiteLLM port,
  mormot.ai.litellm.*) carries NO license (repo metadata `license: null`, no LICENSE
  file) => all rights reserved. A license request is pending; until it is granted,
  that code must not be copied, derived from, or referenced.

  Update procedure:
    gh api repos/flydev-fr/mormot.ai/commits/HEAD --jq .sha        # their new HEAD
    git -C <clone> diff <pinned-sha>..<new-sha> -- mormot2-pgvector # what changed
    # port relevant changes, then update Commit/Date above in the same commit.

