           device attribute numbers), nothing copied: the declarations in
           src/infer/mormot.ai.infer.cuda.pas are written anew. Update: compare
           the entry points used there with a newer cuda.h.

  Kernel compiler (build time only, output checked in): nvcc 13.4.92 (V13.4.92,
           build cuda_13.4.r13.4/compiler.38855100_0) from the same wheel, target
           compute_75, driven by tools/cuda/build-kernels.sh ->
           src/infer/mormot.ai.infer.cuda.ptx.inc. The PTX (ISA 9.4) needs a
           driver for CUDA 13.4 or newer (PTX is excluded from minor version
           compatibility). An older nvcc would widen that, but the CUDA 12
           wheels carry only ptxas and its aarch64 archive does not compile with
           the glibc 2.39 headers of the build machine.

